    aiContent: {
      difficulty: {
        easy: 'Plays legal combinations. No partnership inference. Reveals partner immediately when holding matching Ace.',
        medium: 'Basic climbing strategy (lead strong, save bombs). Infers likely partner from play patterns. Times partner reveal for advantage.',
        hard: 'Full card tracking across 108 cards. Optimal bomb timing. Social deduction: identifies secret partner from play patterns. Coordinates subtly when acting as secret partner. Calculates expected value of reveal timing.',
      },
      considerations: [
        'Hidden partnership creates information asymmetry — AI must model uncertainty about team composition.',
        '108-card dual-deck means duplicate tracking is essential.',
        'Social deduction element requires behavioral modeling of other players.',
        'Bomb management is a critical strategic dimension.',
        'Solo vs partnership decision affects scoring significantly.',
      ],
