          deckDescription: 'Two standard 54-card packs (108 cards total: 2×52 plus 4 jokers). Each pack has 2 to Ace in each suit plus two distinguishable jokers (red and black). In each deal the two Aces of one suit are chosen as Big Aces. Apart from that and red versus black joker, suits and colours are irrelevant for play.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Suits are irrelevant for combinations; they matter only for identifying the matching Big Aces (same rank and suit from the other deck). Red and black jokers are distinguishable.',
          rankDescription: 'For single cards: Big A (highest), Red Joker, Black Joker, then 3, 2, A, K, Q, J, 10 down to 4. Sequences use order A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6-5-4-3-2-A (A high or low). Jokers and Big Aces in sequences count as ordinary Aces. Pairs and bombs rank 3 highest down to 4.',
